  "reason": "The records point in the relevant general direction but do not disclose the later result. R2 establishes in the exact HfNbTaTiZr alloy that lattice distortion and defects suppress electron/phonon heat propagation, directly supporting the scattering component of the mechanism. R1, R4, R5, R12, and R16 show that simulated SRO can materially alter a bcc refractory alloy's local energy landscape, while R3 demonstrates Monte Carlo prediction of chemical ordering on a bcc lattice and R7 connects SRO to ordering transitions and precipitation in another refractory alloy. Other records associate lattice distortion or chemical ordering with altered transport, diffusion, or defect behavior. However, none proposes inducing graded SRO in HfNbTaTiZr, identifies HfTi and TiZr B2-like clusters, predicts their percolation into conductive pathways, or connects those pathways and reduced distortion to an approximately 12% lattice-thermal-conductivity increase and modified high-frequency phonon states. Those specific intervention and mechanism elements would require a substantial new idea."
